{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2853 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "0fe6e75e474a61320ce957873992d68dcd7f953dac2f6c0682d8fa9b01d8d303" :edb/db-before-t 2852 :edb/db-after-t 2853 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536165 50 #inst "2026-10-09T17:48:03.531Z" 13194139536165 true] [17592186105669 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386837 13194139536165 true] [17592186105670 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386844 13194139536165 true] [17592186105670 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386857 13194139536165 true] [17592186106241 1017 #edb/ref 17592186103955 13194139536165 false] [17592186106241 1017 #edb/ref 17592186386851 13194139536165 true] [17592186106241 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536165 true] [17592186106241 1100 "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n$M = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -9\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." 13194139536165 false] [17592186106241 1100 "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." 13194139536165 true] [17592186106241 1145 "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y=3 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx-y=3.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=3+y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=3+y \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3+y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536165 true] [17592186386837 1017 #edb/ref 17592186386838 13194139536165 true] [17592186386837 1089 "q-130922" 13194139536165 true] [17592186386837 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536165 true] [17592186386837 1100 "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 9 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." 13194139536165 true] [17592186386837 1113 #uuid "59028158-753f-502a-bd86-d054f28eae13" 13194139536165 true] [17592186386837 1145 "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 9 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+3y=-1 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx+3y=-1.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=-3y-1,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-3y-1 \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3y-1 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536165 true] [17592186386838 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386839 13194139536165 true] [17592186386838 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386840 13194139536165 true] [17592186386838 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386841 13194139536165 true] [17592186386838 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386842 13194139536165 true] [17592186386838 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386843 13194139536165 true] [17592186386838 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536165 true] [17592186386838 1041 "selection" 13194139536165 true] [17592186386838 1104 #edb/ref 17592186386842 13194139536165 true] [17592186386838 1110 #uuid "e4871325-33a7-51eb-8af2-dcd6a6b97c80" 13194139536165 true] [17592186386839 1034 "\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3y-1 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\\end{aligned}" 13194139536165 true] [17592186386839 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536165 true] [17592186386839 1111 #uuid "c9054393-30f1-5923-b32e-15ea3acad0ba" 13194139536165 true] [17592186386840 1034 "\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1-3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\\end{aligned}" 13194139536165 true] [17592186386840 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536165 true] [17592186386840 1111 #uuid "6bf652d2-fa3b-5fdf-bb1d-6a8462c2431b" 13194139536165 true] [17592186386841 1034 "\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}y-3 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\\end{aligned}" 13194139536165 true] [17592186386841 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536165 true] [17592186386841 1111 #uuid "1382cad3-718b-55f0-a61e-4224134a2cd3" 13194139536165 true] [17592186386842 1034 "\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3y-1 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\\end{aligned}" 13194139536165 true] [17592186386842 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536165 true] [17592186386842 1111 #uuid "1ccd5358-c0ab-5bea-b689-dc701eb72069" 13194139536165 true] [17592186386843 1034 "\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-y-3 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\\end{aligned}" 13194139536165 true] [17592186386843 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536165 true] [17592186386843 1111 #uuid "35b83e50-5a21-54e1-931d-7091856c0a0a" 13194139536165 true] [17592186386844 1017 #edb/ref 17592186386845 13194139536165 true] [17592186386844 1089 "q-42153" 13194139536165 true] [17592186386844 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536165 true] [17592186386844 1100 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+3y=2 \\\\ 3x+9y=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." 13194139536165 true] [17592186386844 1113 #uuid "653d2739-ff74-51ff-bc93-114e79b1a15b" 13194139536165 true] [17592186386844 1145 "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 9 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 9 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+3y=2 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx+3y=2.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=2-3y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2-3y \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2-3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536165 true] [17592186386845 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386846 13194139536165 true] [17592186386845 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386847 13194139536165 true] [17592186386845 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386848 13194139536165 true] [17592186386845 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386849 13194139536165 true] [17592186386845 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386850 13194139536165 true] [17592186386845 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536165 true] [17592186386845 1041 "selection" 13194139536165 true] [17592186386845 1104 #edb/ref 17592186386848 13194139536165 true] [17592186386845 1110 #uuid "639420bc-b662-5eef-8212-3d10fa1e9bbb" 13194139536165 true] [17592186386846 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1-3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139536165 true] [17592186386846 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536165 true] [17592186386846 1111 #uuid "7fa24236-4a87-5b19-82dc-1b1593ea610e" 13194139536165 true] [17592186386847 1034 "No solution" 13194139536165 true] [17592186386847 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536165 true] [17592186386847 1111 #uuid "d1edcbbb-9d9a-5ad0-bde3-3fde951d4a94" 13194139536165 true] [17592186386848 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2-3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139536165 true] [17592186386848 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536165 true] [17592186386848 1111 #uuid "d17a02a7-dc78-59ce-b854-4e616189baa5" 13194139536165 true] [17592186386849 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2+3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139536165 true] [